<% content_for :title, "What Is Domestic & Gender-Based Violence? | Break the Silence" %>

<section class="hero text-center text-white p-5 mb-5">
  <span class="badge-soft"><i class="bi bi-heart-fill"></i> Safe space &bull; Free &bull; Confidential</span>
  <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold">You are not alone.</h1>
  <p class="lead mb-4">Understanding domestic violence and gender-based violence (GBV) in Malaysia is the first step towards safety and support.</p>
  <%= link_to "Get Help Now", hotline_path, class: "btn btn-light btn-lg" %>
</section>

<h2 class="mb-3">What Is Domestic Violence?</h2>
<p>
  Domestic violence is a pattern of abusive behaviour by one person to gain or maintain power and control
  over a family member or intimate partner. It can happen to anyone, regardless of age, gender, religion,
  income level or education.
</p>

<h2 class="mt-5 mb-3">What Is Gender-Based Violence (GBV)?</h2>
<p>
  Gender-based violence is harm directed at a person because of their gender or gender expectations.
  It includes domestic violence but also covers harassment, sexual assault, stalking and other forms
  of abuse that occur at home, at work, in public spaces or online.
</p>

<h2 class="mt-5 mb-3">Types of Abuse</h2>
<div class="row g-3">
  <% [
    ["Physical",  "Hitting, slapping, choking, pushing or any act that causes bodily harm."],
    ["Emotional", "Insults, humiliation, threats, isolation from friends and family, or constant criticism."],
    ["Sexual",    "Any sexual act without consent, including coercion within a marriage or relationship."],
    ["Economic",  "Controlling money, preventing someone from working, or withholding financial support."],
    ["Digital",   "Monitoring phones, stalking online, or sharing private images without consent."]
  ].each do |title, text| %>
    <div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">
      <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h5 class="card-title"><%= title %> Abuse</h5>
          <p class="card-text"><%= text %></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-5 mb-3">Warning Signs</h2>
<ul class="list-group mb-4">
  <li class="list-group-item">Frequent unexplained injuries or reluctance to talk about them</li>
  <li class="list-group-item">Fear of a partner or family member, or constantly seeking their approval</li>
  <li class="list-group-item">Withdrawal from friends, family or activities once enjoyed</li>
  <li class="list-group-item">Having little control over money, phone or movements</li>
  <li class="list-group-item">Sudden changes in mood, confidence or behaviour</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="mt-5 mb-3">Myths and Facts</h2>
<div class="table-responsive">
  <table class="table table-bordered align-middle">
    <thead class="table-light"><tr><th>Myth</th><th>Fact</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>"It is a private family matter."</td><td>Domestic violence is a crime, and everyone has the right to be safe.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>"Only women are victims."</td><td>Women are most affected, but men and children can be victims too.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>"If it were that bad, they would just leave."</td><td>Leaving can be dangerous and difficult because of fear, money, children and social pressure.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>"It is the victim's fault."</td><td>The responsibility for abuse always lies with the abuser.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="alert alert-info mt-4">
  <strong>Need to talk to someone?</strong> Visit the <%= link_to "Hotline page", hotline_path %> for free and confidential support.
</div>